# Deterministic EOLs (the Windows smudge lesson, WS-ERP E6): the source tree
# is LF; `core.autocrlf=true` hosts must not smudge it — otherwise git-apply
# round-trips (the sabotage harness's byte-exact restore) churn CRLF residue
# into the worktree and templates-parity goldens drift CR-only.
*.ex   text eol=lf
*.exs  text eol=lf
*.eex  text eol=lf
*.patch text eol=lf
# The abbrev registry is a BYTE-GOLDEN (the allocator tests assert its exact
# on-disk size) — EOL must be deterministic on every host.
samen_core/priv/abbrev_registry.json text eol=lf
# The templates-parity golden fixtures (the renderer emits LF; the fixtures
# must hold it byte-exactly).
*.golden text eol=lf
# The per-app schema dicts are BYTE-GOLDEN too (each gate diffs the committed
# file byte-exactly against a fresh LF dump) — keep them LF on every host.
schema.dict.json text eol=lf

# B2 payment-file goldens: the USD NACHA byte-golden is LF-exact; the CPA-005
# golden is CRLF-exact and must not be smudged by core.autocrlf.
*.ach text eol=lf
*.cpa005 -text
